goal:
• To develop a critical understanding of the interconnections between globalization and the English language;
• To analyze the changes to the language from new communication technologies, plural speech communities, and transnational economic relationships;
• To develop a familiarity with new modes of literacy, discourse practices, language planning, and teaching;
• To present orally and in writing on topics relating to the above.

1. To provide students with an overview of the conceptual bases of bilingualism and bilingual education;
2. To discuss bilingualism in terms of both psychological (e.g., identity) and social aspects;
3. To discuss the effectiveness of bilingual education, which will help us implement an innovative English language program in Japan;
4. To familiarize students with bilingual education mainly in Japan and the United States.
